    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128501": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (3) a current CV, (4) one or at most two research papers, (5) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (6) teaching evaluations (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002647 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University’s Elliott School of International Affairs and Department of Economics invite applications for two full-time, tenure-track faculty positions beginning Fall 2027. We seek applicants specializing in international trade. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities will include courses for undergraduate and graduate students in the Elliott School and the Economics Department, and the candidate should maintain flexibility regarding the eventual teaching portfolio. The position will be affiliated with the Elliott School’s Institute for International Economic Policy and Master’s programs in International Economic Policy, International Development Studies, and International Science and Technology Policy. Elliott School faculty maintain engagement with policy issues and the policy community as a general criterion for appointment. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in economics with a primary focus on international trade. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or complete all requirements for the Ph.D. by the date of appointment. Applications at the mid-level or senior assistant professor level will also be strongly considered. Advertised Salary: $150,000-$165,000 Other Benefits: GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (3) a current CV, (4) one or at most two research papers, (5) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (6) teaching evaluations (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128100 Applicant Documents Required Documents Statement of Teaching and Research Interest Curriculum Vitae Other Documents Refer to Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter Optional Documents Course Evaluations or Summaries Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
