    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129298": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Comprehensive)",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002673 Academic Title: Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/01/2026 - 06/30/2027, Non-Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University and Capital Medical Group ( CMG ), formerly known as the Medical Faculty Associates, are seeking academic Comprehensive Ophthalmologists for full-time, regular faculty appointments in the Department of Ophthalmology. The positions offer a rare blend of high-quality clinical practice, advanced cataract surgeries, and hands-on education for medical students and residents. Candidates will have the opportunity to develop a high-volume practice to manage comprehensive ophthalmology patients, perform cutting-edge procedures including advanced cataract surgeries, and contribute to training the next generation of ophthalmologists within a collaborative, well-supported environment. The Department of Ophthalmology is part of a growing academic health center located in the heart of a vibrant, world-class metropolitan area with cultural, family, and educational opportunities. These non-tenure-track positions, expected to start as early as Winter 2026, will be filled at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing comprehensive ophthalmology care and performing cataract surgery and other incisional or laser procedures commonly performed by a comprehensive ophthalmologist to a diverse patient population; providing education to the medical students and ophthalmology residents through didactics and clinical and surgical encounters; and contributing to the coverage of the GW Hospital Emergency Department. This call is shared with the other members and paid per night. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Ophthalmology, and license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $250,000 to $375,000 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off and reimbursement for CME , retirement plans with benefits, etc. The Capital Medical Group also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://jobs.uhsinc.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Department Link: https://ophthalmology.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128925 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified or eligible in Ophthalmology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118851": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Dermatology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions in Dermatology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions in Dermatology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants should complete an online application and upload a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. Review of applications will begin on February 28, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002487 Academic Title: Faculty Positions in Dermatology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Dermatology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 5/5/2025-6/30/2026 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 05/05/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington Medical Faculty Associates, an independent, non-profit clinical practice group affiliated with the George Washington University, seeks applicants to fill full-time academic positions in a growing Department of Dermatology in the heart of the nation’s capital. These non-tenure track appointments, expected to start as early as summer 2025, will be made at rank (Instructor or Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching medical students and residents in a variety of clinical and didactic settings, developing an area of specialization in dermatology, and engaging in clinical and/or translational research. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have an MD or equivalent degree, be board-eligible or board-certified in Dermatology at the time of appointment, and be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia, Virginia, and Maryland. Advertised Salary: $175,000 to $300,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants should complete an online application and upload a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. Review of applications will begin on February 28, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Department Link: http://smhs.gwu.edu/dermatology/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/117081 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an MD or equivalent degree at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be board-eligible or board-certified in Dermatology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Are you eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia, Virginia, and Maryland? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street,