    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124808": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002563 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Rank: Assistant Professor, Instructor, Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: General Internal Medicine Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/26-06/30/27 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, seeks full-time academic physicians to join our Division of Primary Care in the Department of Medicine. Join a collaborative and mission-driven team of clinician-educators in downtown Washington, DC. These positions offer a unique opportunity to engage in clinical care and medical education. These non-tenure-track faculty appointments, expected to start as early as July 2026, will be made at a rank (Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing direct, high-quality patient care in an outpatient setting; engaging in population health management and quality/safety initiatives; participating in administrative duties; and contributing to the teaching and mentorship of medical students, interns, residents, fellows, and other learners. All faculty are encouraged to develop scholarly interests and are expected to collaborate with the larger team to enhance access, reduce costs, improve quality, and promote better health outcomes. Faculty can receive up to 10% protected time for research in the first year. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be ABIM -certified or eligible and licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Applicants must also have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth. Advertised Salary: $170,000.00 - $220,000.00 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://medicine.smhs.gwu.edu/general-internal-medicine Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120140 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be ABIM-certified or eligible at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129246": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Research Assistant Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: The Fitzhugh Mullan Institute for Health Workforce Equity, in the Department of Health Policy and Management, is seeking a Senior Research Assistant to work as a data analyst across various projects. The position will support qualitative and quantitative analysis of workforce issues. Specifically, the incumbent will focus on initiatives such as the Health Workforce Diversity Tracker and the SENTRY (Surveillance of Enrollment Trends and Representation Yearly) Monitoring Project. Responsibilities will also include supporting a variety of projects focused on the diversity of the health care workforce. Tasks include cleaning and analyzing federal data sets, creating data visualizations for reports and presentations, and drafting and editing reports and manuscripts. Responsibilities Include: Survey administration and management using Qualtrics and other CRM software (e.g., Salesforce), data collection, data analysis, report generation, data visualization, and helping manage team logistics and communications. Developing monitoring and evaluation tools for the collection, analysis, and dissemination of findings Evaluating large datasets for consistency, completeness, accuracy, and reasonableness Qualitative data collection (e.g., key informant interviews, focus groups) and analysis Cleaning, understanding, transforming, and analyzing datasets with an emphasis on federal datasets Identifying and correcting data entry errors Summarizing results for inclusion in scientific and clientele-oriented publications, including the development of graphs and tables Drafting, editing, and distributing technical publications, reports, and manuscripts Drafting, submitting, and tracking IRB -related functions. Conducting literature reviews Setting up and managing communication with participants and institutions Presenting data findings at conferences, webinars, and briefings Support of Principal Investigator in writing grant proposals Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a BA/BS and 1 year of experience in a related discipline. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: A master’s degree in a related field is desired. Demonstrated interest in social mission, public health, health workforce, healthcare education, or health policy is a plus. Excellent research, writing, and editing skills; Proficiency in or ability to learn Excel, Qualtrics, STATA , SAS , and R within 3 months of hire is desired. Strong project management skills are a plus. Strong knowledge and application of quantitative and qualitative research methodologies is preferred. Excellent communication, analytic, and organizational skills; Sharp attention to detail and ability to deliver high-quality work within deadlines; High degree of professionalism and demonstrated ability to collaborate with cross-sector project partners. Entrepreneurial with the ability to work independently, with a team, and to spark independent project concepts. Preferred additional skills: Experience using Tableau or other data visualization tools is desired. Experience developing concept notes and grant proposals is a plus. Hiring Range $18.51 - $28.21 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Milken Institute School of Public Health (SPH) Family Research and Labs Sub-Family Field Research Stream Service and Support Level Level 3 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 9:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? Yes (University Wide) Posting Number: R002467 Job Open Date: 10/08/2026 Job Close Date: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) * How many years of relevant experience do you have? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
