    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129117": {
      "title": "Hospitalist &amp; Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Hospitalist &amp; Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Hospitalist & Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002663 Academic Title: Hospitalist & Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/01/2026 - 06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University and Capital Medical Group, formerly known as the Medical Faculty Associates, are seeking academic hospitalist psychiatrists for full-time, regular faculty appointments in the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Health. Candidates with fellowship training in consultation-liaison psychiatry are invited to apply. These non-tenure-track positions, expected to start as early as Winter 2026, will be filled at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience, ranging from $280,000 to $320,000. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include serving on the psychiatry hospitalist team, which supports medical-surgery units, the inpatient psychiatric service, and the emergency department; teaching medical students and psychiatry residents; seeing patients in an outpatient setting; and developing a clinical research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in General Psychiatry and license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $280,000 to $320,000 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The Capital Medical Group also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://jobs.uhsinc.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Department Link: https://psychiatry.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128905 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated 