    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129272": {
      "title": "Senior Prospect Analyst, Philanthropic Due Diligence",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Prospect Analyst, Philanthropic Due Diligence Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Prospect Analyst, Philanthropic Due Diligence Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: As George Washington University expands its global fundraising and engagement efforts, the need for consistent and reliable due diligence research continues to grow. Advancement teams are working with an increasingly diverse pool of donors, including individuals, corporations, foundations, and international stakeholders, requiring thoughtful evaluation of potential reputational, ethical, and compliance considerations. The Senior Prospect Analyst, Philanthropic Due Diligence, supports this effort by conducting due diligence research and contributing to review processes. This role helps ensure that decisions related to donor engagement are informed by accurate, well-documented research and aligned with university policies and values. Due diligence activities are currently managed within the Research and Relationship Management team alongside other prospect research and relationship management functions. This role enhances the team’s capacity by providing dedicated analytical support, improving consistency in reporting, and helping manage increasing research volume. Key Responsibilities • Conduct due diligence research on individuals, corporations, foundations, and international entities, including review of reputational, legal, financial, and compliance-related considerations such as adverse media, sanctions, and politically exposed persons. • Prepare clear, structured, and concise due diligence reports that summarize findings and highlight potential risks for internal stakeholders and for the university as a whole. • Support established due diligence workflows, including intake, documentation, and tracking of research requests and outcomes. • Assist in maintaining and applying due diligence guidelines, templates, and documentation standards to ensure consistency and quality. • Collaborate with prospect research, relationship management, and advancement staff to fulfill research requests and provide background information to support donor strategy. • Respond to inquiries from internal stakeholders by providing research findings and clarification within defined processes and guidelines. • Oversee the proposal clearance/clearance to solicit process by managing the process and contributing due diligence research and ensuring relevant information is documented for review. • Utilize internal and external research tools (e.g., LexisNexis, Factiva, Dow Jones, public records) to gather and verify information. • Assist in monitoring emerging risks and flagging findings for escalation to senior team members as appropriate. • Contribute to process improvements and efficiencies within due diligence research workflows. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study.  Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position.  Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: 2+ years of experience in prospect research, due diligence, investigative research, compliance, or a related analytical field is desired. Experience researching individuals, corporate entities, and/or nonprofit organizations. Familiarity with research tools and databases used for due diligence and background research. Experience in higher education, nonprofit fundraising, or advancement environments preferred. Strong research and analytical skills, with the ability to gather, evaluate, and interpret information from multiple sources. Ability to synthesize complex information into clear, concise written reports. Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy and data integrity. Sound judgment and ability to appropriately handle sensitive and confidential information. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple assignments and meet deadlines in a high-volume environment. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to follow established policies, procedures, and workflows. Collaborative approach with the ability to work effectively as part of a team. Hiring Range $58,992.50 - $97,373.72 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: University Advancement Family Dev & Alumni Relations Sub-Family Prospect Management and Research Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Mon- Friday Daytime Hours Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014514 Job Open Date: 10/09/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current employee of The George Washington University? Yes No * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
