    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125949": {
      "title": "Endowed Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Endowed Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Endowed Professor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on July 7, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002537 Academic Title: Endowed Professor of Nursing Rank: Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Nursing Specialty: Contract Type: With Tenure, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 08/01/2025-06/30/2028 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Endowed Professorship in Nursing is responsible for providing support and leadership to the School of Nursing’s ( SON ) academic, research and service missions. A senior-level tenured faculty member, the Endowed Professor is a distinguished scholar with demonstrated success in research, external funding and publications in the areas of health policy, health services and/or nursing workforce research. The Endowed Professor works collaboratively with academic leadership, faculty and staff of the School of Nursing and oversees the Nursing PhD program. This is a full-time 12-month appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor, with a start date as early as fall semester 2025. The Endowed Professor reports to the Associate Dean for Research. All faculty hiring decisions will be contingent upon final approval by the Provost. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include: • Lead and maintain an extramurally funded program of research in health policy, health services research and /or nursing workforce. • Directs PhD in Nursing program • Recruit and mentor PhD students • Teach in area of expertise • Cultivate and lead opportunities for student policy research and initiatives • Strengthen collaborations with external partners with the goal of increasing the impact and dissemination of policy related research • Develops and submits annual reports on the PhD program and overview scholarly productivity of PhD students • Works collaboratively with the Associate Dean for Research and the academic leadership team on the development of early career faculty • Promotes visibility of SON research and scholarship within the school, university, and within local, regional, national and international nursing and healthcare organizations and communities. Minimum Qualifications: • An earned PhD in nursing, public health, public policy or a related field by date of application • Eligible for tenure appointment at the rank of associate or full professor • Demonstrated excellent track record of extramural funding as a Principal Investigator • Experience mentoring doctoral nursing students as well as early career faculty in research and scholarship • Innovative and creative ideas about the future of health policy and related research areas. • Excellent decision-making and problem-solving skills • Evidence of the ability to work and teach in an environment where students, faculty and staff have diverse experiences and perspectives • Strong team leadership and communication skills, excellent interpersonal abilities • Eligibility for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and the Commonwealth of Virginia. Advertised Salary: $150,000 to $190,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on July 7, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120408 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an earned PhD in nursing, public health, public policy or related field by date of application? Yes No * Are you eligible for tenure appointment at the rank of associate or full professor? Yes No * Can you demonstrate an excellent track record of extramural funding as a Principal Investigator? Yes No * Do you have experience mentoring doctoral nursing students as well as early career faculty in research and scholarship? Yes No * Do you have innovative and creative ideas about the future of health policy and related research areas? Yes No * Do you have excellent decision-making and problem-solving skills? Yes No * Can you demonstrate evidence of the ability to work and teach in an environment where students, faculty and staff have diverse experiences and perspectives? Yes No * Do you have strong team leadership, communication skills and excellent interpersonal abilities? Yes No * Are you eligible for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
