    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129212": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy & Cell Biology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy &amp; Cell Biology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy & Cell Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV, cover letter, and teaching statement. Review of applications will begin on September 23, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002640 Academic Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy & Cell Biology Rank: Associate Professor, Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Gross Anatomy and either Histology/Neuroanatomy Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 01/01/2027-06/30/2028 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 01/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Anatomy and Cell Biology at The George Washington University School of Medicine and Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time (12-month) non-tenure-track faculty position at the assistant or associate professor level with a salary commensurate with experience. This position is expected to begin as early as January 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching didactic and laboratory courses in Gross Anatomy and either/Histology/Neuroanatomy. All courses are team-taught with a strong clinical emphasis. Additional responsibilities include engagement in scholarly activities and providing service at the departmental, school, and university levels. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have a terminal degree (PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent) in anatomy or a related field, or must have completed all the requirements for their doctoral degree by the date of appointment. Experience in teaching at the university level is required. Advertised Salary: $125,000 to $180,000 Other Benefits: The George Washington University provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV, cover letter, and teaching statement. Review of applications will begin on September 23, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127478 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a terminal degree (PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent) in anatomy or a related field, or have completed all the requirements for your doctoral degree by the date of appointment Yes No * Do you have experience teaching at the university level? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-850