    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124611": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Plastic Surgery",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Position in Plastic Surgery Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Position in Plastic Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and a cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on April 3, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002593 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Position in Plastic Surgery Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Plastic Surgery Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 7/1/2026-6/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Department of Surgery is seeking a full-time faculty member and plastic surgeon for the Division of Plastic Surgery. We are particularly interested in candidates with a strong commitment to post-traumatic and oncologic reconstruction, with an emphasis on reconstruction of ailments of the breast, extremity, and trunk/perineum, as well as lymphatic and craniomaxillofacial surgery. Academic rank and compensation will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position is expected to begin as early as Fall 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The chosen candidate will provide comprehensive clinical expertise in post-traumatic and oncologic reconstruction, with particular emphasis on breast reconstruction—including oncoplastic, implant-based, and autologous microvascular techniques—as well as extremity, trunk/perineal, lymphatic, and craniomaxillofacial surgery. They will also actively participate in multidisciplinary patient care at The George Washington University Hospital, while teaching and mentoring physician assistant students, medical students, and residents. Additionally, they will engage in scholarly activity and research, and contribute meaningfully to divisional, departmental, and institutional service initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-eligible or board-certified in plastic surgery and fellowship-trained in microvascular surgery or a similar subspecialty at the time of appointment. Applicants must also have demonstrated interest and/or expertise in post-traumatic and oncologic reconstruction and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia. Advertised Salary: $400,000-500,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and a cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on April 3, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://gwhospital.com/services/surgery/inpatient-surgery/plastic-surgery/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124364 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-eligible or board-certified in plastic surgery at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be fellowship-trained in microvascular surgery or a similar subspecialty at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have a demonstrated interest and/or expertise in post-traumatic and oncologic reconstruction? Yes No * Are you eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129233": {
      "title": "Senior Member Service Coordinator",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Member Service Coordinator Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Member Service Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The Division for Student Affairs cultivates an inclusive community that supports connection, growth, and well-being for every student throughout their GW journey. DSA’s integrated approach is to provide a cohesive student experience built upon the core values of genuine collaboration, a compassionate approach, and most importantly, putting students at the center of the work. Campus Recreation, within the Division for Student Affairs, strives to create a space and environment for students to move joyfully, explore different types of physical activity, enjoy constructive competitive opportunities for individuals of all abilities and connect with others in meaningful ways. The home base for programming is the Lerner Health and Wellness Center ( LHWC ). Campus Recreation offers a diverse range of programming opportunities, including intramural sports, club sports, group fitness classes, personal training sessions, fitness clinics and workshops, outdoor education programs, drop-in recreation, and certification courses. This Senior Member Service Coordinator position will report to the Student Development Manager for Campus Recreation and is responsible for: Coordinate and monitor all membership sales, locker rentals, and front desk access control. Identify and pursue opportunities that will improve revenue generation, service quality and operational effectiveness for the facility and its services. Work closely with the Associate Director to review financial reconciliations related revenue collection including memberships, programs and services for Campus Recreation. Manage all aspects of the business operations software system which encompasses a membership CRM , access control, activity registration, equipment rental, online purchasing and payment processing modules. Liaison for GW IT, GWorld and all external groups. Implement a comprehensive marketing plan designed to maximize membership and revenue, while also expanding guest participation and engagement. Lead the development, production, and distribution of physical and digital promotions and external email communications. Coordinate coverage and represent Campus Recreation at various events throughout the year. Develop and delivers training and establishes guidelines for student staff development in the areas of membership sales and guest services. Supervise and evaluate up to 15 Fitness Attendants, 25 Guest Service Attendants, and 1 Marketing Assistant. The position is based at GW’s Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington, DC. The incumbent may be assigned other related duties as needed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Obtained within the first 90 days: CPR / AED /First Aid from American Red Cross or equivalent DC Certified Pool Operator Preferred Qualifications: General knowledge of office management techniques. Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, the Internet, E-mail) and in using standard office equipment. Ability to demonstrate effective communication skills both orally and in writing. Ability to analyze and interpret policy and procedural questions. Ability to research and resolve office management problems and questions. Ability to organize workflow and coordinate activities. Ability to prioritize workload. Ability to update skills on a continual basis. Hiring Range $44,985.20 - $57,788.56 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Student Affairs Family Student Affairs Sub-Family Campus Recreation Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday – Friday 8:30am - 4:30pm with occasional evening or weekend work for Campus Recreation or DSA events Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Telework: No Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014511 Job Open Date: 10/08/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently possess the following certifications? CPR/AED/First Aid certification from the American Red Cross or an equivalent provider DC Certified Pool Operator (CPO) certification Both None * If you do not currently possess one or both of the certifications listed above, are you willing and able to obtain any missing certification(s) within ninety (90) days of employment? Yes No * Do you understand and acknowledge that, if hired, you must obtain any missing certification(s) within ninety (90) days of employment? Yes No Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127629": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Associate Professor of Law Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Associate Professor of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply through the AALS Faculty Appointments Register at https://www.aals.org/services/recruitment/ or complete an online faculty application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 and upload a cover letter indicating the area of interest with a current curriculum vitae, including a list of references. Please email questions to vkarker@law.gwu.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 13, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications submitted either through AALS or GW’s online system will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002641 Academic Title: Associate Professor of Law Rank: Associate Professor Administrative Title: Associate Professor of Law Discipline Law Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Law School invites applications for two entry-level, tenure-track faculty appointments, beginning in Fall 2027. The school is interested in candidates in two fields of study: immigration and family law. The University and Law School have a strong commitment to preparing students to become resilient leaders who help shape solutions to the pressing challenges of our times. The University and Law School also have a strong commitment to recruiting faculty of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the university with different experiences and perspectives. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: This position will be responsible for teaching, research, and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess a J.D. degree or an advanced degree in a relevant field, and have relevant experience such as teaching, legal practice, or judicial clerkships. Applicants must also have a strong academic record that demonstrates the potential for superb teaching and show scholarly promise, evidenced by publications in scholarly journals or scholarly works in progress. Advertised Salary: The salary range for these positions is $185,000–$205,000, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Other Benefits: This position qualifies for healthcare and other benefits available to full-time employees. For more information about these benefits, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Apply through the AALS Faculty Appointments Register at https://www.aals.org/services/recruitment/ or complete an online faculty application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 and upload a cover letter indicating the area of interest with a current curriculum vitae, including a list of references. Please email questions to vkarker@law.gwu.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 13, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications submitted either through AALS or GW’s online system will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Interest Statement of Research Interest Sample Publications List of Publications Course Evaluations or Summaries Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess a J.D. degree or an advanced degree in a relevant field? Yes No * Do you have a strong academic record that demonstrates the potential for superb teaching? Yes No * Do you have relevant experience such as teaching, legal practice, or judicial clerkship? Yes No * Have you shown scholarly promise, as evidenced by publications in scholarly journals or scholarly works in progress? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
