    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129328": {
      "title": "Constituent Records Coordinator",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Constituent Records Coordinator Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Constituent Records Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: This position will assist the Biographical Records team in coordinating and fulfilling complex data processing tasks and projects within the Constituent Records department. Maintains data quality and integrity standards of entered biographical and gift data in Advance, UA’s database of record. Ensures biographical data are properly updated and maintained in Advance, and donations to the university are properly received, entered, and receipted in Advance. The Constituent Records Coordinator handles the day-to-day processing and recording of constituent data in compliance of departmental procedures, policies and governmental regulations as all impact data integrity, records management, gift processing, and donor confidentiality. Exercise a high level of independence with a focus on accuracy and reliability of constituent biographical and gift data. Identify reactive data entry research needs. Review, process, and enter biographical data for constituents into Advance, including address changes, e-mail and telephone updates, committee participation, and philanthropic interests. Review and process gifts into the Advance database and the university’s on-line giving platform (Luminate) and payment gateway (GiveCampus). Assist in the remote deposit of checks and authorization of credit cards through point-of-sale machine. Demonstrates a high commitment to quality with strong judgement skills. Duties include: Enter biographical data for constituents into Advance, including address changes, email and telephone updates, committee participation, philanthropic interests, etc. Act as a liaison with other University Advancement departments, as well as other university administrative offices to provide recommendations for procedural changes and in other matters pertaining to biographical and gift records. Solicit updated constituent information from university colleagues and retrieve updated information submitted voluntarily from alumni through websites, emails, mail, phone calls, and other university contacts. Monitor the flow of biographical entry requests to make certain that deadlines are met. Provide daily monitoring of correspondence through organization email accounts, and respond promptly to data change requests from alumni, university staff, and internal clients. Identify and execute Biographical Records’ data projects that impacts and requires partnerships with other units in University Advancement and GWIT to fulfill. Assist the Director, Biographical Records, with data-integrity checks through quality and auditing reviews. Assist in training of staff on processing constituent records data. Follow departmental procedure, university policies, and governmental regulations as all impact data management, data integrity, gift processing, and donor confidentiality of records maintained by the university. Make recommendations for procedural changes to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of processes that impact biographical and gift records, in order to better to support the university’s advancement efforts. Perform other work-related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: University Advancement Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 40 Hiring Range 23.00 Work Schedule: Monday- Friday, 830am-5pm Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T001325 Job Open Date: 10/13/2026 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is your expected hourly range? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
