    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129464": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: a cover letter describing interest in and qualifications for the position; a curriculum vitae including a detailed description of teaching experience, service experience, and scholarly publications including those related to biology education; a 2-page statement of teaching philosophy; copies of official student evaluations from past courses taught; and the names and contact information for three referees who can comment on your classroom instruction. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002665 Academic Title: Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Rank: Teaching Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Special Service, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 08/01/27-05/31/30 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences at The George Washington University invites applicants for a position as a Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology to begin as soon as Fall 2027. This is a full-time, renewable, Specialized Service contract position with a course load of 3 courses per semester (Fall and Spring). The initial renewable appointment period will be for 3 years. Because this is a teaching position, there are no research expectations, but the candidate will be required to contribute some effort towards service for the University and maintain knowledge in the discipline sufficient to support teaching. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The primary responsibilities of the candidate will comprise the design, delivery, and supervision of undergraduate courses associated with our non-majors Introductory Biology sequence to offer content in areas such as cellular biology, microbiology, nutrition, physiology, and evolution to multiple large lecture sections each semester. The candidate will manage and coordinate labs associated with the non-majors Introductory Biology lectures while collaborating with our teaching faculty, laboratory managers, graduate teaching assistants, and undergraduate teaching assistants to ensure a high-quality educational experience that prepares undergraduate students for advanced coursework and to be scientifically literate citizens. There may also be opportunities to rotate into majors Introductory Biology and/or an upper-division course related to the candidate’s area of expertise depending on departmental needs. In addition, the candidate will have the opportunity to collaborate with educational consultants and instructional technology specialists through the Center for Teaching Excellence ( https://library.gwu.edu/about-center-teaching-excellence ) to receive professional development in evidence-based pedagogy, course (re-)design, active learning, effective assessment practices, etc. Office space will be provided in Bell Hall, where the teaching labs for our Introductory Biology courses are housed. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have completed a Ph.D. in Biological Sciences or related discipline by the time the appointment begins and must have experience teaching a combination of lecture or laboratory courses as instructor of record at the university level. Advertised Salary: $75,000-$80,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits . Other Information: Questions about this position may be directed to the Chair of the search committee, Dr. J. Aidan Manubay at jmanubay@gwu.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: a cover letter describing interest in and qualifications for the position; a curriculum vitae including a detailed description of teaching experience, service experience, and scholarly publications including those related to biology education; a 2-page statement of teaching philosophy; copies of official student evaluations from past courses taught; and the names and contact information for three referees who can comment on your classroom instruction. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Department Link: https://biology.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129028 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Names and Contact Information for References Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD in Biology or a related discipline, or will you have completed the requirements for the PhD by the time of appointment? Yes No * Can you demonstrate experience teaching a combination of lecture and laboratory courses as the instructor of record at the university level? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129477": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, Sigur Center",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Program Coordinator, Sigur Center Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Program Coordinator, Sigur Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: About Us The George Washington University Elliott School of International Affairs ( ESIA ) is one of the world’s leading schools of international affairs and one of the largest schools of international affairs in the United States. Located in the heart of Washington, D.C., its mission is to educate the next generation of international leaders, conduct research that advances understanding of important global issues, and engage the policy community in the United States and around the world. About the Center The Sigur Center for Asian Studies is a university research institute and the academic home of the Asian Studies Program of the Elliott School of International Affairs at the George Washington University. Its mission is to increase the quality and broaden the scope of scholarly research and publication on Asia, promote US-Asian scholarly interaction and educate a new generation of students, scholars, analysts, and policymakers. The Sigur Center promotes research and policy analysis on East Asia, Northeast Asia, Southeast Asia, and South Asia through an active program of publishing, teaching, public events, and policy engagement. About the Program Coordinator Role As the Program Coordinator for the Sigur Center, you’ll report directly to the Center Director and Assistant Director to keep the Sigur Center running smoothly. As a core team member, you’ll lead the execution of ~30 annual events, workshops, and VIP delegation visits, while driving our outreach, communications, and the Visiting Scholars Program. You will also provide occasional support to constituent programs within the Sigur Center, including but not limited to the Taiwan Education and Research Program ( TERP ), and collaborate with other institutes within the Elliott School and partners throughout GW for co-sponsored events and activities. Specific Responsibilities: Event Coordination & Outreach Coordinates the Center’s special events and programming under the guidance of Center leadership: Creates promotional materials and graphic assets for outreach. Oversees venue booking, catering, staffing, and event schedules. Interfaces with key public and private partners to drive audience engagement. Tracks event metrics for internal reporting and provides support for co-sponsored events. Expected to attend all events to handle on-site logistics (event set-up, technology, cleanup, etc.). the main point of contact with internal GW partners (IT, Venues team, etc.) and outside vendors. May also provide support for co-sponsored events. Communications & Digital/Social Media Coordinates the Center’s website, content creation, accessibility, and publications. Coordinates with other Center staff on communications tools, platforms ( EMMA , WordPress, social media), including SEO /optimizing social networking and email marketing. Program & Scholar Support Supports the Center’s Visiting Scholars (~15–20 annually) program. Handle intake and visa procurement, the scholar’s orientation, their required event or publication, their offboarding, and their inquiries. As needed, assists Director and Assistant Director with writing, editing, and formatting annual reports for stakeholders. Administrative & Operations Support May assist with delegating duties for up to three student assistants. Under the guidance of the Assistant Programs Director, processes payments and honoraria, reimbursements, and reconciles procurement card charges in a timely manner. Team Support & Collaboration As a key member of a small, high-impact team, you will contribute to our varied priorities to ensure the evolving needs of the Sigur Center and our programs are met. May be called upon to support Elliott School-wide activities. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. We believe in the power of in-person collaboration and the flexibility of remote work. This is a hybrid position, based at GW’s Foggy Bottom campus in Washington, D.C. The schedule typically involves three days in person and two remote days per week – though the schedule may change based on program needs and priorities such as in-person events. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED plus 3 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: About You The ideal candidate will bring a combination of skills, background, and enthusiasm, including: Enjoys day-to-day program coordination, administrative operations, and creating a welcoming, inclusive environment for students, scholars, colleagues, and visitors. Skilled in and energized by coordinating events, workshops, or meetings; experience planning student activities or community outreach initiatives is a plus. Experience with—or a strong interest in learning—website content management systems (such as WordPress), email marketing platforms (such as EMMA ), social media management. Proactive communicator who asks thoughtful questions, checks in on shifting priorities, and knows when to seek guidance. Tech-savvy with standard business platforms (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Zoom Workplace). Strong writing, editing, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to distill complex information clearly across digital platforms. Thrives in the details and gets a genuine sense of satisfaction from keeping moving parts organized, on schedule, and running smoothly. Exposure to project management tools (e.g., Asana, Trello, Notion) or digital organizational methods is a plus. Bachelor’s degree in a related field (such as International Affairs, Asian Studies, Communications, or Public Policy) is preferred. Experience living, studying, or working in Asia and/or familiarity with a modern Asian language is a plus. If you are energized by planning events, building clear communications, and engaging with global scholars and leaders, we encourage you to apply. We welcome applications from recent graduates and early-career professionals eager to learn, grow, and contribute to a vibrant academic community. Hiring Range $21.80 - $28.32 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Elliott School of International Affairs (ESIA) Family Academic Affairs Sub-Family Program Administration Stream Service and Support Level Level 3 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM. Schedule may vary based on special events or other Center needs. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014531 Job Open Date: 10/22/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: 11/30/2029 Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129488": {
      "title": "Assistant Program Director, Marketing360",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Program Director, Marketing360 Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Program Director, Marketing360 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The F. David Fowler Career Center ( FDFCC ) supports GW Business students and alumni in developing the skills, knowledge, and connections needed to navigate their careers. Through career programming, guidance, employer and alumni engagement, and experiential learning, the Center connects students with opportunities to explore career paths, build skills, and gain experience. Marketing360 is a career development program for undergraduate and graduate students interested in marketing. The program helps students understand the range of career paths available in marketing, build technical and professional skills, and develop relationships with alumni and industry professionals. Programming includes workshops, networking, industry engagement, and experiential learning. The Assistant Program Director, Marketing360 leads the day-to-day management and continued development of the program. The role combines program operations, student-focused communications and engagement, external relationship building, experiential programming, and career guidance. Marketing360 culminates in cross-functional, semester-long pro bono projects that allow students to apply what they have learned to real-world client challenges in a team-based environment. Key Responsibilities Include: Program Management and Development Manage the day-to-day operations and ongoing development of Marketing360, ensuring programming, communications, events, and student experiences are organized, timely, and aligned with program goals. Design and deliver a two-semester program that helps undergraduate and graduate students explore marketing career paths, build technical and soft skills, and develop professional networks. Plan and execute workshops, presentations, networking events, site visits, and other student-facing career development activities. Develop clear, engaging, student-focused messaging and communications to promote programming, opportunities, expectations, and resources. Manage program operations, including budgets, contracts, scheduling, logistics, records, student participation, communications, and other administrative processes. Coordinate the Marketing360 pro bono project experience, including project planning, student teams, client communication, timelines, and logistics. Oversee student workers supporting the program and manage program resources, presentations, guides, templates, and other student-facing materials. Track participation and career-related outcomes and use data and feedback to evaluate the program and improve delivery. Identify and implement process improvements that strengthen program effectiveness and the student experience. Collaboration and Relationship Building Build and maintain relationships with industry professionals, employers, alumni, and other external partners to create a strong pipeline of speakers, mentors, networking opportunities, and pro bono project partners. Identify and cultivate new relationships that expand students’ exposure to marketing careers, industries, organizations, and professional opportunities. Maintain strong relationships with Marketing faculty and identify opportunities to connect academic learning with career exploration and professional development. Partner with colleagues across the Fowler Career Center and GW School of Business to strengthen student programming and identify opportunities for collaboration. Student Career Advising Provide individualized career advising to undergraduate and graduate students across industries. Help students assess their interests, skills, and goals and identify appropriate marketing career paths and opportunities. Mentor students on resumes, interviewing, professional branding, networking, and other career-readiness skills. Connect students with relevant career resources, alumni, employers, and other opportunities. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. This is a hybrid position with a combination of on-campus and remote work. The role requires regular on-campus presence for student programming, meetings, events, and other responsibilities. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Experience in marketing, marketing communications, career development, higher education, program management, or a related field is desired. Demonstrated experience managing programs, projects, events, or other complex initiatives with multiple stakeholders and deadlines. Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail. Strong fluency with office and productivity technology, including Google Workspace and Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint and/or Canva. Ability to think strategically while operating effectively as an independent contributor and managing day-to-day execution. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain productive relationships with external professionals, employers, alumni, faculty, and other stakeholders. Experience developing and delivering workshops, events, or other student-facing programming. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to develop clear and engaging student-focused communications. Experience with career coaching, student advising, talent development, or related areas preferred. Experience with data collection, program assessment, and reporting preferred. Hiring Range $58,992.50 - $97,373.72 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: School of Business (SB) Family Student Affairs Sub-Family Career Services Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 9:00 A.M. - 6:00 P.M. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014532 Job Open Date: Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) * Which areas of marketing do you have direct professional experience in (e.g., brand strategy, digital marketing, marketing analytics, or content creation)? Please indicate the number of years of experience you have in each area. (Open Ended Question) * Rate and describe your proficiency level with Microsoft Suite including Docs, Sheets, PowerPoint, Chat and Calendars (e.g., basic data entry vs. advanced formulas, pivot tables, and reporting). (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe a situation where you demonstrated initiative, resourcefulness, and effective communication while working with a team. What was your contribution, and what was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
