    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129509": {
      "title": "Corcoran Marketing and Communications Manager",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Corcoran Marketing and Communications Manager Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Corcoran Marketing and Communications Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: George Washington University is seeking a Communications and Marketing Manager to advance and support the strategic priorities of its Corcoran School of the Arts & Design. The Communications and Marketing Manager is responsible for creating and executing comprehensive communications and marketing strategy that positions the Corcoran School as a leader in the arts and art scholarship, advances its organizational brand, and manages its voice in public-facing materials. Responsibilities include directing, managing, and implementing internal and external communications and strategy for the school’s academic divisions, partnerships, community engagement initiatives, events and exhibitions. The manager will help shape and iterate messaging across communications channels, including social media, websites, newsletters, advertising campaigns and marketing collateral. The manager will also work with the schools’ senior leadership on messaging and critical external and internal communications, as well as event promotion and creation of video content to engage and inform key stakeholders. The manager will also build and maintain close relationships with faculty to identify and promote stories of impact and innovation. This is a position for a proactive, responsive and motivated individual willing to work within a dynamic educational and programmatic environment, and contribute to the broader institutional vision. Performs other work related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. About the Corcoran School of the Arts & Design GW’s Corcoran School of the Arts and Design is dedicated to educating the next generation of cultural leaders. Part of the Columbian College of Arts and Sciences, the school functions as an incubator for artists, designers and scholars, who learn from internationally renowned faculty at the intersection of creativity and social innovation. The school has seven program areas that offer undergraduate and graduate degrees in art history, design, interior architecture, museum studies, music, fine arts, theatre and dance. Its home in Washington, D.C., means students work and study at some of the city’s most prestigious companies, galleries and museums. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study.  Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position.  Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: A Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization and at least 2 years of relevant professional experience. Superior oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage social media platforms. Demonstrated ability to create, edit, monitor, and promote a wide range of content. Experience with online content management systems. Demonstrated skill in developing printed or digital collateral including providing guidance and direction or executing design, video, or other photography work. Advertising and marketing expertise. Hiring Range $66,095.67 - $90,896.59 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Safety and Operation Family Comm, Mktg & Media Sub-Family Communications and Public Relations Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM. Occasional evenings and weekends. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014536 Job Open Date: 10/23/2026 Job Close Date: 10/30/2026 If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * Briefly describe your relevant professional experience. (Open Ended Question) * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129517": {
      "title": "Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: GW’s School of Nursing (GW Nursing) drives innovation and improvements in healthcare worldwide through the education of compassionate nurses, esteemed educators and researchers, entrepreneurial leaders, and influential policy experts. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement is responsible for coordination of clinical and field experience placements of students enrolled in the Post-Master’s Certificate ( PMC ), MSN , and DNP programs. This role serves as the liaison between School of Nursing ( SON ), GW SON students, and clinical partners, and maintains a strong relationship with the local healthcare community. The incumbent will initiate, negotiate and review contracts for execution between the university and our clinical affiliates, support students in their searches and tracking their compliance items. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement position requires strong interpersonal skills, attention to detail, critical thinking, and be able to work autonomously. This position will report to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement position will collaborate with Clinical Placement team members in the assignment of clinical sites, as well as provide support for students needing clinical or field placements. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement will process requests, communicate requirements and steps to students, assist with data collection, maintain relationships with faculty, and present clinical placement policies and procedures to ensure that clinical placements are processed and obtained. Responsibilities include: Works independently to process clinical and field experience requests for PMC , MSN , & DNP students. Cultivates and sustains good relationships with preceptors and sites and maintains preceptor and clinical site databases. Coordinates and performs record keeping and correspondence related to clinical/practicum experiences for all graduate nursing students. Organizes and participates in orientation sessions and other educational workshops. Works in collaboration with the program leadership to ensure program-specific information is communicated with students. Responsible for initiating, negotiating and executing affiliation agreements/contracts between GW SON and external clinical site/partners to ensure compliance with university regulations. Monitors student compliance through compliance tracking system. Coordinates clinical activities, create clinical reports tracking student clinical experiences in the clinical management program as required for accreditation. Assists with data collection, sets up data sets, and provides periodic data analysis to identify opportunities for process and outcome improvements. Develops and facilitates effective working relationships and communication as well as providing quality service with both internal and external constituents, clinical sites/preceptors. Effectively utilizes the clinical management system/program to manage all aspects of the clinical placement process, including but not limited to student placements, evaluation, documentation, and reporting as needed to meet CCNE and program standards. Develops and maintains tracking systems and databases to ensure the efficient and effective management of administrative and clinical activities, and provides proactive reporting analysis to leadership and clinical curriculum committee. Participates in the CCNE accreditation meetings and on-site evaluation. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Ashburn, Virginia College/School/Department: School of Nursing Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 40 Hiring Range $18.40 - $28.81 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T001337 Job Open Date: Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: No Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is your expected hourly range? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
