    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129454": {
      "title": "Digital Multimedia Specialist",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Digital Multimedia Specialist Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Digital Multimedia Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: GW Engineering seeks a Digital Multimedia Specialist to advance the strategic mission of the School of Engineering and Applied Science by creating and collecting content to share our stories and messages across a variety of multimedia platforms. Working collaboratively with the Director of Communications and Marketing, the MarCom team and other stakeholders, the Digital Multimedia Specialist works to elevate the academic reputation, enrollment efforts, alumni engagement, research enterprise, and connect the GW Engineering community of students, faculty, staff and alumni with high-quality visual information and experiences. Graphic design, video and photo capture, and editing are key elements of this position. They plan and implement visual storytelling that engages key internal and external audiences, creating and amplifying authentic and inclusive brand-reaffirming messages and thought leadership. The individual creates and implements a strategic social media calendar, developing content that amplifies timely and appropriate messages to key audiences through key media. They manage software and digital filing/ sharing of content. Core relationships within the school include the Dean’s office, the marketing and communications team, administrative colleagues across academic departmental leadership, graduate enrollment and admissions, undergraduate enrollment and admissions, student-facing roles and Development and Alumni Relations. Within the university, this role collaborates with GW Creative Services and GW Advertising, and other departments to produce visual storytelling. The position reports to the Director of Communications and Marketing and should specialize in visual/creative content creation and provide strategic vision associated with creation of marketing deliverables used in print, web and multimedia applications throughout the school of engineering. The role performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Additional Responsibilities are: Plans and implements through visual storytelling that engages key internal and external audiences, creating and amplifying authentic and inclusive brand reaffirming messages and thought leadership. Plans and manages through execution, graphic design and video production for the school in a creative, collaborative and inclusive team environment. Strategizes and executes on a timeline, co-managing the content calendar, collaborating with team members managing social media, web and other earned and owned media. Manages software and digital filing/ sharing of content, recommending software and equipment as needed. Measures outcomes to determine future shifts in creative direction, strategy, and tactics. Oversees graphic design, content capture and editing, communications and multimedia to achieve department’s goals and maintain consistency across offices and departments. Regularly will capture content with school equipment (photo, video, audio) to leverage content production. Follow the AP Style Guide, the GW Brand Guide and integrate brand personality as appropriate; and manage permissions for displaying personas in the content. Perform in a hybrid position located within the GW School of Engineering and Applied Science in Washington, D.C., just two blocks from the Foggy Bottom Metro (Orange, Silver, Blue) and collaborate with the GW Marketing and Communications team located a few blocks away in “Western Market” at 2000 Pennsylvania Ave. Performs other work-related duties as requested. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the lead from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: 2+ years of successful experience in graphic design, digital media, video and photo editing, creative design and website design. Project management experience preferred. Demonstrated knowledge and experience with key video and photo editing software. Candidates should share professional social media profiles to demonstrate experience managing enterprise accounts. A background in marketing and communications, leveraging digital marketing tools and software to amplify authentic messaging and storytelling that is informative and/or persuasive. Successful experience in visual storytelling across multiple social media channels. Strong organizational and operational skills to oversee and complete multiple complex projects working in parallel. Experience in marketing in higher education is preferred, but not required. Exceptional judgment and the ability to interact effectively with a diverse population at all levels, facilitate decision-making and maintain a positive and constructive demeanor treating all staff, students, faculty, alumni and vendors with professionalism, courtesy and respect. II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: School of Engineering and Applied Sciences (SEAS) Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 40 Hiring Range $18.40 - $30.00 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T001329 Job Open Date: 10/13/2026 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is the hourly rate you are looking to make? Please provide a range below. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
