    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129498": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Neurobiology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty applicationand upload the following documents: I. a cover letter describing qualifications and fit within the department (1 page); II. a curriculum vitae including a full list of publications and of references; III. a research statement (2 pages); IV. a teaching statement (1-2 pages); V. three recent publications; and VI. a list of names and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Please contact Dr. Damien O’Halloran at damienoh@gwu.edu, Chair of the Neuroscience Faculty Search Committee, with any questions. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002666 Academic Title: Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Neurobiology Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences at The George Washington University ( GWU ) invites applicants for a tenure-track faculty position in Neurobiology at the rank of Assistant Professor, to begin as early as Fall 2027. The Department of Biological Sciences brings together investigators using diverse experimental systems and cutting-edge molecular, cellular, genomic, physiological, and computational approaches to address fundamental questions in biology. The Department has broad strengths spanning neuroscience, anatomy and physiology, cell and molecular biology, immunology, developmental biology, evolution, ecology, and organismal biology. The department seeks a candidate with complementary expertise who investigates fundamental questions in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models, including but not limited to neural development and function, neurophysiology, neurobiology of behavior, neuroimmune interactions, and neural regeneration and repair . Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an externally funded research program that integrates graduate and undergraduate students and investigates basic cellular and molecular questions in neurobiology. The successful candidate will also strengthen our multidisciplinary teaching program by teaching a course in Molecular Biology and a new course for our Neuroscience major, related to the successful candidate’s area of expertise. Minimum Qualifications: Required Qualifications: (1) a completed PhD in neurobiology or a closely related field; (2) research expertise in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models; (3) at least 2 years of postdoctoral experience at the start of the position; and (4) research accomplishments as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications. Advertised Salary: $90,000-$96,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for GW’s full-time employee benefits package. For more information on GW’s benefits visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits Other Information: Abundant opportunities exist for interdisciplinary research and collaboration across the Department, the Columbian College of Arts and Sciences, the GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences, and the broader George Washington University community. The University’s location in Washington, DC provides opportunities for collaborations with federal agencies, research institutes, hospitals, and biomedical organizations, including the National Institutes of Health, the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, Children’s National Hospital, and other institutions within the region’s exceptionally strong biomedical research community. Faculty can also engage with GW’s interdisciplinary research centers and programs spanning neuroscience, biomedical sciences, computational biology, immunology, and translational medicine. The Department provides access to a diverse and accomplished community of undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, as well as opportunities to mentor trainees through GW’s interdisciplinary graduate programs. The Department of Biological Sciences is committed to building a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive intellectual community in which faculty, trainees, and staff can thrive. We value scientific innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration, excellence in teaching and mentorship, and the inclusion of diverse perspectives that strengthen our research and educational missions. Office and laboratory space will be located in GWU’s Science and Engineering Hall, a newer building on campus which opened in January 2015 ( https://www.gwu.edu/research- resources#Discovery) and offers state-of-the-art imaging and nanofabrication facilities. Our location in Washington, DC offers exceptional undergraduate and graduate mentorship opportunities through proximity to the National Institutes of Health, Janelia Research Campus, the Smithsonian Institution and a consortium of DC-area universities. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty applicationand upload the following documents: I. a cover letter describing qualifications and fit within the department (1 page); II. a curriculum vitae including a full list of publications and of references; III . a research statement (2 pages); IV. a teaching statement (1-2 pages); V. three recent publications; and VI. a list of names and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Please contact Dr. Damien O’Halloran at damienoh@gwu.edu, Chair of the Neuroscience Faculty Search Committee, with any questions. Department Link: https://biology.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129027 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Statement of Research Interest Sample Publications Names and Contact Information for References Optional Documents List of Publications Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a completed PhD in neurobiology or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have research expertise in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models? Yes No * Will you have at least 2 years of postdoctoral experience at the time of the appointment? Yes No * Do you have research accomplishments as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129508": {
      "title": "Financial Systems BI Analyst",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Financial Systems BI Analyst Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Financial Systems BI Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The Financial Systems Bl Analyst ( FSBIA ) delivers financial accounting, financial planning, and budgeting data deliverables, data stewardship, subject matter expertise, and IT liaison support for the Controller’s Office, Financial Management, and University Budget Office customers within the Finance Division. The Financial Systems Bl Analyst position will coordinate with various stakeholders and user groups to: Gather and analyze requirements and promote the correct interpretation, documentation, visualization, and use of data related to various enterprise data needs. Map requirements into dashboards, answers, and reports while ensuring conformance to all enterprise standards. Conduct data quality checks and perform data cleaning, as needed, to support data governance and improve data quality across enterprise systems. Plan, integrate, and configure business and technology solutions to support the business priorities of the Finance Division. Work closely with GWIT partners and across Finance in the development of systems automation and financial reporting solutions. Serve as a subject matter expert and internal consultant. The ideal candidate is someone who enjoys working with end users on the front-end of business intelligence and automation tools and is excited to further develop their technical ability. The primary functions of this role are: This position works with the Director of Business Intelligence Services and the Director of Financial Systems and Solutions to understand the institutional data and reporting needs of the Finance Division in order to design and develop data visualizations and dashboards and respond to ad-hoc data requests from staff. This position will work with GWIT to deliver efficient process automation solutions. This position will work directly with Business Intelligence Services and coordinate with other IT organizations and campus partners in the use of the University’s reporting and process automation technologies, as well as plan and execute continuous improvement. Serving as an adviser and participates in the planning and execution related to the deployment of data deliverables and/or other process improvement efforts. Utilizing a creative and analytical skill set to work in partnership with internal and external partners, along with senior management, supporting the delivery of process automation initiatives. Design, implement, and support business intelligence dashboards and data visualizations, including providing support for ad-hoc data requests in collaboration with the various stakeholders across the Finance Division. These efforts will include data from the University Data Warehouse, the enterprise financial system, and other systems in accordance with institutional data governance policies, standards, practices, and procedures. Performs other work-related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Background in accounting, financial planning, or corporate finance with an understanding of higher education financial, administrative, and student data is strongly preferred. CPA , CMA , or other professional accounting designation is a plus but not required. 2+ years of experience developing financial reporting, including developing dashboards and data visualizations, and reports using business intelligence software tools such as Tableau or Power Bl is desired. Experience with one or more data technologies (e.g., Oracle, SQL Server, etc.) is preferred, and a willingness to learn how to leverage these technologies to support operational solutions, technical prototypes, and proofs-of-concept. Experience with data warehouse modeling, creating, managing data structures, and ETL data flows is strongly preferred. Experience in supporting Budgeting and Enterprise Performance Management tools is a plus. Ability to triage a situation and create a prototype to support decision-making is desired. Strong interpersonal and leadership skills; facilitating discussions between business stakeholders and technologists to challenge, build consensus, negotiate, and resolve conflicts Experience with various SDLC methodologies, such as Waterfall and Agile (Scrum) is preferred. Understanding emerging technologies and how to deploy them to create innovative services. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Hiring Range $64,048.99 - $118,899.97 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Ashburn, Virginia College/School/Department: GW IT Family Information Technology Sub-Family IT Business Intelligence Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5.00 p.m. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014535 Job Open Date: 10/23/2026 Job Close Date: 11/02/2026 If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience using Tableau or Microsoft Power BI? (Open Ended Question) * Are you comfortable with Excel at an intermediate to expert level using pivot tables and v-lookups? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have accounting experience combined with demonstrated hands-on experience in data analysis, financial modeling or general ledger, month end close, financial reporting or GAAP compliance? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129510": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Career Counseling",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Director, Career Counseling Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director, Career Counseling Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: Established in 1865, The George Washington University Law School is the oldest in Washington, DC. The school is accredited by the American Bar Association and is a charter member of the Association of American Law Schools. The law school is located on the GW campus in the downtown neighborhood familiarly known as Foggy Bottom. The Career Development Office of The George Washington University Law School advises and counsels law students in professional development and assists them in job search strategies. This position presents a rewarding opportunity to help law school students and recent law school graduates begin their legal careers. The Assistant Director, Career Counseling provides individual counseling to J.D. students on all aspects of career planning, including self-assessment, career exploration, job application materials, interview preparation, and professional skills development. This position will report to the Director, Career Counseling and Professional Development in the Career Development Office with the following representative duties and responsibilities: Assists J.D. students in determining career goals and objectives through self-evaluation. Assesses students’ articulated career interests and recommends avenues of exploration to meet their career goals. Advises and counsels students on all matters related to career and professional development and the legal job search process. Refers students to mentors and other professional contacts as appropriate. Serves as an advisor in the Inns of Court program and assists with program coordination and delivery of program content. Learns of employment opportunities, and shares them with students and Career Center staff. Works with students on the full life-cycle recruitment process for an entry-level attorney, J.D. advantage, and professional positions, including resume and cover letter review, interview preparation and follow-up, and job offer evaluation. Collaborates with the Employer Outreach Team to ensure student preparedness for participation in recruiting programs and professional activities such as networking events. Develops and conducts skills development workshops on all components of the job search process, such as resume and cover letter writing, developing a network of professional contacts, special applications and interviewing skills, and job search resources. Develops written informational materials on basic career guidance issues such as resume and cover letter writing, networking, and interviewing, as well as informational materials on specific practice areas for which this position has responsibility. Organizes and implements seminar programs, workshops, and panel discussions on a variety of legal and alternative career topics, both independently and in conjunction with alumni and student groups. Participates in marketing and promotion of Career Development Office programs and services to students, alumni, and employers, including through social media and newsletters. Maintains positive relationships with employers, alumni, students, staff, and faculty. Serves as a resource to student organizations and faculty on the career and professional development of students. As required, represents the Career Development Office at national, regional, and local meetings of appropriate professional organizations and associations, and periodically interfaces with law career counselors at other law schools. Assists with the programming, coordination, and delivery during all phases of networking fairs, job fairs, recruitment programs, and other career development programs, which may include travel. Works on special projects as assigned by the Director of Career Counseling and Professional Development and the Associate Dean, Career Development Office. Performs other work-related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: J.D. plus two years of experience at a law firm, legal search firm, or in-house legal department post-admission to a state bar or the District of Columbia Bar are strongly preferred. Counseling experience with law students or young lawyers. Career planning, guidance, and mentorship skills. Understanding of basic coaching techniques. Knowledge and understanding of career practices and opportunities within local, national, and global legal communities. Excellent presentation skills in live and virtual settings. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Hiring Range $58,992.50 - $97,373.72 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: GW Law School (LAW) Family Student Affairs Sub-Family Career Services Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm; Evenings & Weekends Required Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014537 Job Open Date: 10/23/2026 Job Close Date: 10/26/2026 If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129526": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The Senior Administrative Assistant provides administrative support to the Office of Undergraduate Affairs and Special Programs and the Office of the Provost. The position reports directly to the Assistant Provost for Administration and Operations. This experienced administrative support position provides enhanced administrative support to one or more individuals. This position coordinates schedules and maintains calendar(s) for assigned staff, regularly prioritizing and arranging meetings, conferences, and appointments. This role also typically monitors and assists with budget preparation and record keeping, maintains and reconciles P-cards for departmental, institutional, or work unit accounts, and anticipates and prepares background materials as needed. This position may compose reports related to the status of department budgets or project funding requirements. The position typically monitors and approves travel, procurement, conference, honoraria, consultant, and other expenses associated with department needs and sponsored projects. The Senior Administrative Assistant will: Provide general administrative support to the Associate Provost for Undergraduate Affairs and Special Programs, and other senior leaders within the Office of the Provost Answer calls, respond to inquiries from students, parents, alumni, faculty, staff, and administrators; make photocopies; maintain spreadsheets and databases; submit and monitor FixIt requests; and greet visitors Schedule, plan, and set up events and meetings, including room reservation and tech support coordination with GW IT and catering purchases Draft and circulate meeting notices and agendas, take meeting notes and track meeting deliverables Generate reports from GW databases including Tableau and Banner. Collect, maintain, and update office databases and documents in Box Assist with Provost Office events including the annual Academic Honors Ceremony; planning the event; collecting, sorting, and verifying records of eligible students using internal dashboards; and coordinating with the offices of University Events and Academic Planning and Assessment Project management, research, data collection, and report preparation regarding undergraduate academic programs in areas such as academic integrity, academic policy, and program development Support the Special Programs with administrative processes when needed Update and maintain documents related to faculty hiring, promotion, and leave applications; assist with instructor recruitment for Special Programs within GW and regionally Order office supplies and manage inventory Prepare receipts and reports for P-card processing; invoicing, expensing, and reimbursement processing Coordinate travel, including flight arrangements, hotel bookings, and schedules for the Associate Provost and visitors Resolve routine administrative issues with other units The position is based at GW’s Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington, DC. The incumbent may perform other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED plus 3 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study.  Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position.  Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Outstanding customer service skills, detail-oriented, and acquires new skills quickly Ability to work proactively and exercise good judgment Strong writing skills and reading comprehension Fluent in software such as Microsoft Office, Adobe Acrobat, Gmail, Google Workspace, Box, and GW enterprise systems such as Banner, Oracle, Kronos (time reporting), and iBuy (expense reporting) Able to use and maintain general office equipment, inventories of supplies and equipment, and office files Able to assist with the general functions of an academic campus and office Able to work independently and complete routine tasks without additional guidance Hiring Range $21.80 - $28.32 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Academic Affairs Family Administration Sub-Family Administrative / Operations Stream Service and Support Level Level 3 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 9 am-5 pm Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Telework: No Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014435 Job Open Date: 10/13/2026 Job Close Date: 10/31/2026 If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
